puddle doctor (puddle 0.1.0, windows x86_64)

ok    CPU virtualization    on in firmware
FAIL  Hypervisor            Windows Hypervisor Platform is off
      fix:  Enable the Windows Hypervisor Platform feature in PowerShell as administrator:
              Enable-WindowsOptionalFeature -Online -FeatureName HypervisorPlatform -All
            then restart Windows. (Or: Settings > System > Optional features > More Windows
            features > Windows Hypervisor Platform.) Virtual Machine Platform, which WSL2 uses,
            is a different feature.
      from: WinHvPlatform.dll: The specified module could not be found. (os error 126)
info  Code integrity        memory integrity (HVCI) on; App Control policy for programs off
ok    Bundled runtime       msb 0.7.7-puddle.2 (C:\Users\dev\AppData\Local\Programs\puddle\runtime\msb.exe)
FAIL  Runtime starts        msb can't load a DLL it needs (0xC0000135)
      fix:  msb links the Windows Hypervisor Platform's DLL: fix "Hypervisor" above first.
skip  Test boot             not checked: no usable hypervisor
ok    Disk space            120 GB free on the drive that holds Puddle's data (/home/dev/.local/share/puddle)
info  Guest kernel          the guest kernel of the Windows runtime has /dev/mem
      note: Puddle works. Root in a sandbox can map the virtual devices' registers through
            /dev/mem, so the runtime's own checks on every register access are the only line
            there. The Linux runtime's guest kernel is built without /dev/mem.
ok    Disk encryption       data drive encrypted (BitLocker); swap /dev/dm-1 encrypted (BitLocker)
ok    SSH agent             the agent on \\.\pipe\openssh-ssh-agent holds 2 keys (ed25519: 1, rsa: 1)
ok    Azure CLI (az)        version 2.64.0
ok    Credential store      a test write and delete worked
ok    Global Secure Access  client not installed

2 problems to fix before Puddle can run sandboxes. (1.2 s)

